1
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:50,884
‪I now unveil here for you, the
‪heartwarming love letter of Hwagyeongdang,

3
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,803
‪who was a great poet
‪and painter of her era.

4
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,306
‪[attendees exclaiming]

5
00:00:57,766 --> 00:00:59,350
‪[Hwa-yong laughs]

6
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,737
‪[ghostly shriek]

7
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,281
‪[screaming, clamoring]

8
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:20,330
‪If this was found in the process
‪of relocating Kang Pyeong-gun's tomb,

9
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:23,083
‪would that then mean this love letter
‪was in his coffin as well?

10
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,877
‪Yes. How heart-wrenching.

11
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,254
‪It's romantic, don't you think so?

12
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:31,049
‪Are long-term cold cases
‪really your specialty?

13
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:31,966
‪Yeah.

14
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:34,636
‪How would you like another?

15
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:38,056
‪One that's been cold for over 300 years.

16
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,099
‪Me and you.

17
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:45,647
‪[upbeat music playing]

18
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,001
‪EPISODE 6

19
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:17,679
‪[Gang-uk] <i>‪A couple of ground rules</i>
<i>‪before we start working together.</i>

20
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,889
<i>‪Rule number one: We share everything,</i>

21
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:22,058
<i>‪and we never go to a scene alone.</i>

22
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,019
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Rule number two:</i>

23
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:28,648
<i>‪We keep a safe distance</i>
<i>‪when we're on the move.</i>

24
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:36,531
<i>‪Rule number three:</i>

25
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:40,493
<i>‪We always leave at least one seat</i>
<i>‪between us when we sit down.</i>

26
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:49,752
‪So, let me see if I got everything.

27
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,963
‪A male ghost appeared during an event

28
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:55,592
‪unveiling a 300-year-old love letter
‪that was found

29
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:57,802
‪while workers relocated an ancient grave.

30
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,471
‪Three hundred? My goodness.

31
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,891
‪You weren't lying.
‪That was a really long time ago.

32
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:07,478
‪So what can you tell me about the ghost
‪who appeared in front of you?

33
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,147
‪He's an artist, actually.

34
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:13,318
<i>‪The one who painted</i>
<i>‪Hwagyeongdang's portrait at Yeeon.</i>

35
00:03:13,401 --> 00:03:16,321
‪[Gang-uk] <i>‪Well, I guess all we need to do</i>
<i>‪is find his remains, right?</i>

36
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,866
‪Not really.
‪He's not the one we should go after.

37
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,368
‪We should look for Hwagyeongdang.

38
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,746
‪Wait, he wrote the letter, right?

39
00:03:24,829 --> 00:03:26,331
‪I don't get it.

40
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:28,499
‪What's the point of looking
‪for someone else's remains?

41
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,251
‪The thing is…

42
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:34,172
‪what Dowon told me was a whole different
‪story than the one we heard.

43
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:36,174
‪[pensive music playing]

44
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,467
‪[birds chirping]

45
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:14,629
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Apparently,</i>
<i>‪Kang Pyeong-gun, who was of royal blood,</i>

46
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:17,924
<i>‪started pursuing Hwagyeong,</i>
<i>‪even though she was Dowon's lover.</i>

47
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:20,593
‪-[Kang Pyeong-gun] What have you found?
‪-He's a painter named Dowon.

48
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,178
‪He and Hwagyeong grew up together.

49
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,806
‪His name means nothing.
‪I care not what it is.

50
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:27,809
‪All that matters is my Hwagyeong.

51
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,561
‪She's mine.

52
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:32,939
‪And I must come up with a plan

53
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:36,484
‪to ensnare him
‪and draw Hwagyeong to my side.

54
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,279
‪I told you to come down a thousand times!

55
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,531
‪You wretched woman,
‪why do you refuse to listen?

56
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:45,493
‪Do you intend to mock me to the very end?
‪Damn you! You insolent--

57
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:46,786
‪Who are you? Wait!

58
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:47,912
‪[onlookers gasp]

59
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,498
‪[noble 1] Good heavens! This man…
‪This man is attacking a nobleman!

60
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:53,376
‪-[noble 2] How dare he! A nobleman!
‪-[noble 1] He's attacking a nobleman!

61
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:58,631
‪-Help me, please! He tried to kill me!
‪-Please! Wait! Please don't hurt him!

62
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,591
‪[bureaucrat] <i>‪Assaulting a nobleman.</i>

63
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,927
<i>‪With the right connections</i>
<i>‪at the police bureau,</i>

64
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,929
<i>‪they can turn it into a crime</i>
<i>‪against the social order,</i>

65
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,222
<i>‪one punishable by death.</i>

66
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,395
‪[sobbing] Let him go.

67
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:15,356
‪Don't do this to him, I'm begging you!
‪Stop it, please!

68
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:18,401
‪Stop! Please, stop!

69
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:23,740
‪[officer] Halt!

70
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:27,118
‪[Hwagyeong whimpering]

71
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:32,957
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Kang Pyeong-gun's</i>
<i>‪obsession turned into madness.</i>

72
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:39,047
<i>‪He held Dowon's life over her head</i>
<i>‪until she had no choice but to marry him.</i>

73
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,810
‪[panting]

74
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:57,231
‪Where are you bound in such a hurry?

75
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:02,195
‪How dare you.

76
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:04,947
‪You tried to deceive me,
‪and you will answer for it.

77
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,034
‪[gasps]

78
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:11,788
‪No! Wait!

79
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:17,710
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Hwagyeong attempted to escape</i>
<i>‪Kang Pyeong-gun's tyranny,</i>

80
00:06:18,294 --> 00:06:19,378
<i>‪but she was brutally murdered</i>

81
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:21,047
<i>‪-before Dowon's eyes.</i>
‪-No!

82
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:23,424
‪[sobbing]

83
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,553
‪Forgive me, dear.

84
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:36,437
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Kang Pyeong-gun went so far</i>
<i>‪as to hide Hwagyeong's death.</i>

85
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:40,274
<i>‪After taking an empty palanquin</i>
<i>‪to Mount Geumgangsan,</i>

86
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:42,485
<i>‪he spread the ridiculous rumor</i>

87
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:45,446
<i>‪that Hwagyeongdang had disappeared</i>
<i>‪into the mountains.</i>

88
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:50,618
<i>‪To this day, no one knows</i>
<i>‪where she was actually buried.</i>

89
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,413
‪[sighs]

90
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:57,458
‪Hold on a second. Do you think Dowon
‪could have been lying to you?

91
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:00,002
‪The way I see it,

92
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:03,631
‪when it comes to romantic relationships,
‪you have to hear both sides of the story.

93
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:08,094
‪Besides, Hwagyeongdang's love letter
‪was found in Kang Pyeong-gun's tomb, so…

94
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:10,513
‪He said there's evidence
‪that could prove that wrong.

95
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:13,766
‪Can you look into that?
‪That's in the "living department."

96
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,810
‪So it's right up your alley.

97
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:19,730
‪[Gang-uk sighs]

98
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,315
‪[Yeo-ri]
<i>‪By the way, I was doing some research</i>

99
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:24,485
<i>‪and it turns out Dowon didn't get</i>
<i>‪recognition during his lifetime,</i>

100
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,697
<i>‪but he was later recognized as</i>
<i>‪an important artist thanks to Hwajeopdo.</i>

101
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,949
‪-[Gang-uk sighs] This place is kinda…
‪-[crows cawing]

102
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,955
‪[sighs] I don't know,

103
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:38,416
‪I think this feels more like
‪Cheon Yeo-ri's department, actually.

104
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:42,044
‪Oh, wow.

105
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:44,213
‪What if Dowon was wrong?

106
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:46,257
‪[clicks tongue]

107
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:50,094
‪[yelps]

108
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,513
‪Oh! [exhales]

109
00:07:54,932 --> 00:07:56,058
‪Hello, sir.

110
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,769
‪What's with the sickle?

111
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:02,023
‪[crows squawking]

112
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,569
‪So, what did you say you were looking for?

113
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:09,530
‪Yes, I'm here
‪because I heard there's a relic

114
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:12,492
‪of the painter Dowon that was passed
‪down through this family.

115
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:13,743
‪-Yeah.
‪-Hmm.

116
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:32,595
‪[sighs]

117
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:36,849
‪Excuse me, sir.
‪May I take a look at this too?

118
00:08:58,496 --> 00:08:59,580
‪Hmm?

119
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:02,083
‪[dramatic music playing]

120
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,363
‪So it turns out the two love letters
‪were actually just one.

121
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:35,700
‪That's right. And she didn't write it
‪for Kang Pyeong-gun either.

122
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:36,659
‪She wrote it for Dowon.

123
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:41,330
‪[sighs] I thought this was
‪the Joseon-era version of <i>‪Ghost</i>‪,

124
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:43,374
‪but this guy is just a psychopath.

125
00:09:43,457 --> 00:09:47,044
‪A fake empty palanquin? That was the best
‪he could do? So much for royal blood.

126
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,589
‪-[scoffs]
‪-You know what? I think that's why.

127
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,382
‪It's because he was royalty.

128
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:53,426
‪He couldn't stand
‪the fact that her heart wasn't his.

129
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,345
‪I want to find Hwagyeongdang

130
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:59,015
‪and reunite her with Dowon
‪once and for all.

131
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:03,185
‪This whole thing has been keeping her
‪bound to Kang Pyeong-gun for far too long.

132
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,021
‪We have to figure this out.

133
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:15,281
‪Don't be like that, please.

134
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:17,825
‪You're not going
‪to walk away now, are you?

135
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:22,580
‪We're in too deep already.
‪Even if I wanted to back out, I couldn't.

136
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:28,336
‪The thing is, the prosecution caught wind
‪of what happened last time, you know?

137
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:30,921
‪And we struggled to keep it under wraps.

138
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:33,382
‪So I've been thinking,
‪at least until things settle down--

139
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:36,427
‪-Mrs. Ok--
‪-Anyway, that Ju Sin-ho painting

140
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,970
‪-you gave me last time really helped…
‪-[phone buzzing]

141
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,972
‪Excuse me. It's Cheon Yeo-ri.

142
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:41,724
‪What does she want?

143
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:45,227
‪Hello, Ms. Cheon. [laughs]

144
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:48,230
‪We're talking a lot lately,
‪aren't we, huh?

145
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:52,568
‪Ah! Of course.
‪Okay, sure. See you tomorrow.

146
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:59,367
‪You don't think Cheon Yeo-ri
‪could've caught on to something, do you?

147
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:00,660
‪No, no way.

148
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:04,288
‪Well, I'll find out
‪when I meet with her, I guess.

149
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:06,957
‪[sighs]

150
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:11,253
‪Yes, so in other news, I'm meeting
‪with Yeeon's director tomorrow.

151
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,922
‪I'm going to see
‪if anything else comes up.

152
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,299
‪Hmm. Okay, no worries.
‪I'll join you after work.

153
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,552
‪Hmm? I can go there by myself, you know.

154
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,845
‪Uh, you can't do that.

155
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:22,014
<i>‪Remember rule number one?</i>

156
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,141
‪We have to share everything we learn,

157
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:27,061
‪and we can't go to a scene alone,
‪that's what we agreed on.

158
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:29,021
‪And besides, we have
‪a team dinner afterward.

159
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:31,357
‪Team dinner?

160
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:34,610
‪Yeah. We've earned it
‪after all this hard work.

161
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:36,987
‪[laughs] That pork rind place again?

162
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,991
‪Ah. That sounds pretty good.
‪To be safe, I'll bring an extra shirt.

163
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:43,828
‪[laughs]

164
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,165
‪Well, by the way, um,

165
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:52,962
‪I wanted to do a little more digging
‪before asking, um… Mmm…

166
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:55,798
‪Where did the artwork on display
‪in the Reina Hotel come from?

167
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:59,385
‪Oh, the artwork.
‪Um, our art team handles all of that.

168
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:03,514
‪We usually get them through
‪Gallery Cheon, which my aunt runs.

169
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:07,476
‪Why?

170
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,979
‪Is there a problem, or…

171
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,480
‪Oh, no, no. Don't worry about it.

172
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,483
‪It's not that there's anything wrong
‪with Reina or Gallery Cheon.

173
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:18,237
‪It's just that Reina's name came up
‪during an art distribution investigation.

174
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,201
‪ACQUISITIONS
‪AND TRANSACTION RECORD

175
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,245
‪OF ARTWORK PLACED IN HOTELS

176
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:29,081
‪Are these all the art pieces
‪Reina has on display right now?

177
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:30,374
‪Yes.

178
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,043
‪I sent each of the transfer files
‪separately to your email.

179
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,171
‪Great, so what I need now

180
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:38,215
‪is a list with all the artwork
‪Reina has purchased

181
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,342
‪through Gallery Cheon
‪over the past ten years.

182
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:42,595
‪Check all the market values
‪against what we paid.

183
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,264
‪Bring that over to me
‪once you're done, Mr. Bong.

184
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,058
‪And don't tell anyone. No one can know.

185
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:52,146
‪Got it.

186
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:07,036
‪I'm busy, what do you want?

187
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:08,078
‪Have a seat.

188
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:09,997
‪What is it?

189
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:15,002
‪So… about the Reina Hotel case
‪you mentioned, how's that going?

190
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:18,547
‪-Again with this artwork stuff?
‪-I'm just curious, don't be like that.

191
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:20,508
‪Whatever. What exactly do you wanna know?

192
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:23,802
‪You said someone started digging
‪and got shut down. Who was it?

193
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:29,141
‪[sighs] Whatever, no point in hiding
‪anything from you anyway.

194
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:33,812
‪So originally, Nam Ji-hun
‪from Unit Three was looking into it.

195
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:36,315
‪Then the higher-ups
‪told him to shut it down.

196
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:37,233
‪Now I'm doing it.

197
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,777
‪If the money's gone,
‪that's probably laundering.

198
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:42,947
‪But since the artwork disappeared,
‪bribery's more like it, isn't it?

199
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:45,157
‪Well, yeah, that's
‪what I've been thinking too.

200
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:49,036
‪But why would the Chief Prosecutor
‪do the dirty work himself? I don't get it.

201
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:50,037
‪Exactly.

202
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,915
‪I also thought that was weird.
‪That's why I'm looking into it.

203
00:13:52,998 --> 00:13:54,875
‪There's a lot I don't know,

204
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:56,544
‪but at least I know
‪where the money went now.

205
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,006
‪Reina, right?

206
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,052
‪You're acting weird.

207
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:06,720
‪You're obsessed with Reina.

208
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:08,138
‪You're up to something, aren't you?

209
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,599
‪I'm not up to anything. What do you mean?

210
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,143
‪I'm completely swamped
‪just dealing with my cold cases.

211
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:14,228
‪[inhales sharply]

212
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,439
‪Well, okay. So it's not Reina? Is that it?

213
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:18,649
‪It's not Reina.

214
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:20,734
‪[exhales]

215
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:22,570
‪I'm going there later. Wanna come with me?

216
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:25,406
‪I can't. I have somewhere to be.
‪Great work, by the way.

217
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:29,410
‪[Seo-hyeon] Hey. [scoffs]

218
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,370
‪Well, that's surprising.

219
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:33,581
‪You're more of a romantic
‪than I thought, Ms. Cheon.

220
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:36,292
‪Of course it's interesting to me,
‪I mean, they're my ancestors.

221
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:40,254
‪But why are you so emotionally invested
‪in a love letter from that long ago?

222
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:41,797
‪-[both chuckle]
‪-You're right, I know.

223
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:45,593
‪It's not the romance.
‪There's more to it than that.

224
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:49,096
‪It felt like the words of someone who
‪was anticipating something, you know?

225
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,389
‪A final farewell.

226
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:53,267
‪I don't know why,
‪but it really stuck with me.

227
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:57,438
‪I wonder where Hwagyeongdang
‪was buried. I'm really curious.

228
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,772
‪I just don't get it.

229
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,734
‪Why would someone with as much
‪on your plate as you, Ms. Cheon,

230
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,611
‪be so curious about something like that?

231
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:06,071
‪[both chuckle]

232
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:09,533
‪Well, if there's anything you'd like
‪to know that isn't in the public records,

233
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:14,204
‪you might want to check out the alma mater
‪of my late father, the founding chairman.

234
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:17,791
‪All the records related
‪to Kang Pyeong-gun were donated

235
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:20,753
‪to the Yeeon Museum,
‪so they're all in one place.

236
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:24,548
‪We're planning to donate the letter too,
‪once it's officially unveiled.

237
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,425
‪-[both chuckle]
‪-[knock on door]

238
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:28,177
‪-Yes?
‪-[door opens]

239
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,971
‪-Oh, Mr. Kang.
‪-Hi, sorry I'm late.

240
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:33,474
‪-Just made it back from the airport.
‪-Oh, not at all.

241
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,809
‪You made it just in time. Have a seat.

242
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:37,811
‪We were just catching up over the phone.

243
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:42,024
‪That's right. She told me you were coming,
‪so I insisted on joining.

244
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:44,151
‪[Hwa-yong]
‪The trip here must've been so tiring.

245
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:46,695
‪-[Min-hwan] Not at all.
‪-[Hwa-yong] Oh, my goodness.

246
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:51,784
‪[exhales]

247
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:53,410
‪[Seo-hyeon] Gang-uk?

248
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,915
‪-Um, what?
‪-"Um, what"?

249
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,375
‪Hey, what are you doing here?

250
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,168
‪What are you doing here?

251
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,632
‪[Yeo-ri]
‪You and Ms. Lee seem pretty close.

252
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:08,175
‪[Min-hwan] Oh, she's close with my mother.

253
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:12,262
‪Anyway, talk about good timing.
‪I almost missed you there.

254
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,431
‪Where are you coming in from?

255
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,559
‪They found some artifacts
‪at the Baekhyeon Leisure Town site

256
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,353
‪so they had to stop construction.

257
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:21,522
‪-Hmm.
‪-I went there to sort things out.

258
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:23,816
‪-Hmm.
‪-Oh.

259
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:28,946
‪For you.

260
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:32,866
‪W-What's this?

261
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:41,375
‪I was on a business trip in Europe
‪and I thought they'd suit you.

262
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:49,550
‪Thank you. No one's
‪given me gloves before.

263
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:52,761
‪They're lovely.

264
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:54,013
‪Mm-hmm.

265
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,725
‪You're not here
‪because of what I said, are you?

266
00:16:57,808 --> 00:16:58,809
‪What do you mean?

267
00:17:00,602 --> 00:17:02,229
‪Ah, this is where
‪the money went, isn't it?

268
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,607
‪I get it now.
‪That's why you're here so often.

269
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:08,610
‪I know something's up.
‪What is it? Just say it.

270
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:12,072
‪-Spit it out, come on. What?
‪-Ah, it's nothing. Nothing's going on.

271
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,576
‪-Hey, wait for me!
‪-Hey, don't do that.

272
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:16,994
‪[Seo-hyeon] Oh, come on.

273
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,664
‪-Just for a minute.
‪-Get off me.

274
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:31,800
‪-So we meet again.
‪-So we do.

275
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:36,597
‪Oh. I know you.
‪You're the famous Cheon Yeo-ri, right?

276
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,724
‪Nice to meet you. Uh…

277
00:17:38,807 --> 00:17:42,144
‪I'm Prosecutor Im Seo-hyeon. Prosecutor Ma
‪and I work at the same district office.

278
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,647
‪I saw the article about you two,
‪by the way.

279
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:47,608
‪Uh, congratulations.

280
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:49,443
‪So when's the, um, engagement ceremony?

281
00:17:51,403 --> 00:17:55,032
‪Oh. That would've been amazing.

282
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,034
‪But they just published
‪a follow-up article.

283
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,661
‪-Sadly, they were just rumors.
‪-[Seo-hyeon] Oh, really?

284
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,579
‪[sighs]

285
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,664
‪Huh. Uh…

286
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,625
‪We're going to grab some dinner.
‪Why don't you join us?

287
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:06,460
‪When did I say yes to that?

288
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:08,754
‪[Seo-hyeon] Oh, come on. You always
‪have dinner by yourself anyway.

289
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:09,880
‪[groans]

290
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:12,508
‪Let's call it a team dinner
‪so it's an excuse to eat together.

291
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:14,927
‪Right? Let's go together.

292
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:17,554
‪Come on, just forget it.
‪Uh, let's just… let' s get out of here.

293
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:19,098
‪That sounds good.

294
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:24,561
‪Let's go. Together.

295
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:26,939
‪The four of us.

296
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,364
‪[Seo-hyeon laughs] Look at this.

297
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:39,034
‪Check this out. We took this
‪the last time we came here.

298
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:42,204
‪Whoa. You two have
‪the couple selfie thing down.

299
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,872
‪That's… That's not a couple selfie.

300
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:46,792
‪Im insisted we take a picture since we
‪were here, so I just went along with it--

301
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,001
‪Well, you look good together.

302
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:50,170
‪[footsteps approaching]

303
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:51,296
‪[clears throat]

304
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,050
‪Thank you.

305
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,344
‪All right, let's have a toast then.
‪Our beers are here.

306
00:18:58,053 --> 00:19:00,347
‪-Sure.
‪-Cheers!

307
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,476
‪Oh, come on…

308
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,271
‪[gulps, sighs]

309
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:12,401
‪Ah. I feel like you had to tone down
‪the meal because of us, so I…

310
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,360
‪I feel bad.

311
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,445
‪You know, since we work
‪for the government,

312
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:17,489
‪we have no choice
‪but to follow public service rules

313
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:19,032
‪so we have to pay separately.

314
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:21,285
‪The pasta here is really good.

315
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:24,079
‪And the ramen too, it's good.

316
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:26,123
‪-You eat ramen often?
‪-Mm-hmm.

317
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:29,918
‪Sometimes I do.
‪It's a good quick meal, very convenient.

318
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:32,838
‪[Seo-hyeon] Oh, really? I always thought
‪people from <i>‪chaebol</i>‪ families

319
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:34,506
‪only ate specially prepared meals,

320
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,758
‪fancy fine dining, 12-course feasts
‪and all that kinda stuff.

321
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,135
‪[chuckles]

322
00:19:38,218 --> 00:19:40,846
‪So, if you like ramen,
‪we should have it by the Hangang River.

323
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:43,348
‪It tastes even better
‪when you're by the riverbank.

324
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:46,560
‪I can't wait to go there
‪and have some ramen with you two.

325
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:48,478
‪Can you just… just, you know… just…

326
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:49,563
‪[Seo-hyeon] What'd I say?

327
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:51,190
‪What about you, Prosecutor Ma?

328
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:54,651
‪Have you ever had ramen
‪by the Hangang River?

329
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,403
‪-Yeah, well--
‪-Oh, he lives for it.

330
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,822
‪Back when
‪we worked at the Southern District,

331
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:01,408
‪we ran into each other while jogging
‪the day after a team dinner,

332
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:04,703
‪got ramen for our hangovers,
‪and went to the office together.

333
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:08,415
‪I didn't know people
‪ate ramen for hangovers.

334
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:11,001
‪I'll have to try that out,
‪you know, at some point.

335
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:12,878
‪That's nice.

336
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:14,213
‪Just let me know when, I wanna try it too.

337
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:15,214
‪What?

338
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,758
‪Of course. Let's do it. It's a plan.

339
00:20:17,841 --> 00:20:19,927
‪Ramen by the river,
‪the four us. [chuckles]

340
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:36,610
‪There. Have some.

341
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:40,530
‪-My goodness.
‪-Eat it, come on.

342
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:41,907
‪Go ahead.

343
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:47,454
‪[choking]

344
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,081
‪Oh…

345
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,543
‪[coughing]

346
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:05,264
‪-You did that for me, Gang-uk?
‪-No, just… eat.

347
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:10,644
‪Are you okay with beer?
‪You don't like it that much.

348
00:21:10,727 --> 00:21:12,604
‪[Yeo-ri chuckles] I drink beer sometimes.

349
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,984
‪You really surprised me there.

350
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:19,695
‪You're a lot more thoughtful
‪than I thought you'd be, Prosecutor Ma.

351
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:21,863
‪Judging by the way
‪you treat Prosecutor Im,

352
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,657
‪it's safe to say you're pretty caring.

353
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,866
‪[scoffs]

354
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,702
‪Well, if I'm being honest,
‪he surprised me too.

355
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:28,870
‪I didn't know Gang-uk had a sweet side.

356
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:30,080
‪[Gang-uk] I wasn't being thoughtful.

357
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:32,124
‪I was just worried
‪she'd spill the food all over herself.

358
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:35,043
‪-She's really clumsy, actually--
‪-Exactly, and that was thoughtful.

359
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,465
‪-[sighs]
‪-You love me.

360
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,676
‪What? No, I don't. Waiter?

361
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:45,345
‪Can we get another round here, please?

362
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:50,309
‪Oh. You're the designated driver, right?

363
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:51,893
‪-[driver] Yes, hi.
‪-There you go, thanks.

364
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:54,479
‪-Sure.
‪-Where'd you park? I can give you a ride.

365
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:56,189
‪It's fine.
‪I'll go get my car in the morning.

366
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:57,733
‪-I'll take a cab.
‪-[phone buzzing]

367
00:21:57,816 --> 00:22:00,277
‪-[Seo-hyeon] You sure?
‪-Mm-hmm. Later.

368
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,946
‪-All right, see you tomorrow.
‪-[Gang-uk] Bye.

369
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:06,700
‪Well, next time, we'll meet up
‪by the river for ramen.

370
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,997
‪-[engine starts]
‪-Thanks again, sir.

371
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:20,339
‪-I'll give you a ride.
‪-Oh. It's all right.

372
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:23,425
‪Uh, I think I'll just…
‪I'll just walk home.

373
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:24,843
‪To get some fresh air.

374
00:22:26,803 --> 00:22:28,597
‪Can I walk you there?

375
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:30,724
‪[chuckles softly] That's okay.

376
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:35,395
‪-Get home safe.
‪-Mm-hmm.

377
00:22:43,361 --> 00:22:44,696
‪[engine starts]

378
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:56,750
‪Oh, no. That's not the right department.
‪Don't send that to them. Yeah.

379
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,835
‪Oh, I'll… I'll call you back tomorrow,
‪okay? Bye.

380
00:23:00,378 --> 00:23:04,299
‪Yeo-ri, what did Ms. Lee say?
‪Any developments or anything?

381
00:23:04,382 --> 00:23:06,384
‪-No developments.
‪-Oh.

382
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:09,888
‪By the way, that was a close call, right?
‪I did good, didn't I?

383
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:12,057
‪Yeah, that was really nice of you.

384
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,517
‪Im sure loved it.

385
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,143
‪I didn't do it for Im, you know.

386
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,479
‪I was just looking out for you, Yeo-ri.
‪Don't you get it?

387
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:20,148
‪That doesn't make any sense, does it?

388
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,734
‪Im Seo-hyeon is the one
‪who would be affected if we touched.

389
00:23:23,568 --> 00:23:26,154
‪And Min-hwan was right,
‪you were thoughtful and sweet.

390
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:27,614
‪Sweet? Don't say that, Yeo-ri.

391
00:23:27,697 --> 00:23:30,283
‪You know that's not fair, come on.
‪If I'm being honest here,

392
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:33,495
‪I was so busy watching Min-hwan
‪being sly, and trying to manage Seo-hyeon,

393
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:36,164
‪I couldn't even tell if the pasta
‪was going through my mouth or my nose.

394
00:23:43,046 --> 00:23:43,880
‪Wait, Yeo-ri.

395
00:23:45,215 --> 00:23:47,134
‪-Are you a little bit--
‪-Of course I'm not.

396
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:51,471
‪Ah, I didn't finish.
‪How do you know what I was gonna say?

397
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,640
‪Whatever you say, my answer won't change.

398
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:06,653
‪[upbeat, romantic music playing]

399
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:53,116
‪Did my hands touch you?

400
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:56,745
‪Um, I'm not sure. But I don't think so.

401
00:25:13,803 --> 00:25:16,681
‪Uh, since your accident,

402
00:25:17,807 --> 00:25:19,726
‪have you ever done something like this?

403
00:25:21,228 --> 00:25:22,312
‪This is my first time.

404
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:26,816
‪Uh, and I think, as far as I know,

405
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,653
‪only my hands trigger the effect.

406
00:25:29,736 --> 00:25:30,862
‪Good. I think we're fine, then.

407
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:33,281
‪And if not, I'm totally okay with it.

408
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:36,159
‪Uh, please just… don't worry about it.

409
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:37,494
‪So, for now…

410
00:25:38,411 --> 00:25:41,665
‪uh, let's just keep an eye on you.

411
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:44,209
‪If you don't see anything by tomorrow,

412
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:45,710
‪then I guess you should be in the clear.

413
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,921
‪You really don't have to worry, Yeo-ri.

414
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:49,965
‪It's fine. We'll just handle things
‪as they come.

415
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:53,426
‪Still, if you see something,
‪give me a call.

416
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:55,011
‪Okay.

417
00:26:06,314 --> 00:26:08,358
‪He won't see them. He won't see them.

418
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:09,818
‪Of course he won't see them.

419
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:12,779
‪He's not calling,
‪but he shouldn't be calling anyway.

420
00:26:12,862 --> 00:26:14,155
‪-He's not gonna see them.
‪-[phone buzzing]

421
00:26:14,239 --> 00:26:15,407
‪He's not-- [gasps]

422
00:26:16,908 --> 00:26:17,867
‪Do you see a ghost?

423
00:26:18,827 --> 00:26:21,621
‪No. I don't see them.
‪I'm calling to let you know.

424
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:23,748
‪[sighs]

425
00:26:23,832 --> 00:26:25,709
‪Oh my gosh, you scared me.
‪I thought you saw a ghost.

426
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:27,627
‪I said call me
‪if you see anything, didn't I?

427
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:30,880
‪[stammering] I'm sorry.

428
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:36,094
‪[sighs]

429
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:14,049
<i>‪-You shouldn't meet him.</i>
‪-[shouting]

430
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:18,386
‪-Come out. Show yourself! Who's there?
<i>‪-…choice. I have to do it for the clan.</i>

431
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:21,306
‪[character] <i>‪Come on, there's</i>
<i>‪gotta be something else we can do.</i>

432
00:27:21,389 --> 00:27:23,933
‪-[panting]
‪-<i>‪Wait. I just thought of something!</i>

433
00:27:29,105 --> 00:27:31,149
‪-[phone buzzes]
‪-[gasps]

434
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:37,113
‪Yep, hello?

435
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:39,407
‪How about now?

436
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,035
‪I'm a little worried.

437
00:27:42,118 --> 00:27:44,245
‪Oh. Pretty sure I don't see anything.

438
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:46,748
‪At least not yet.
‪I'm gonna call you if I do.

439
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:52,337
<i>‪-Gang-uk…</i>
‪-Yes?

440
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:53,963
‪This isn't gonna work.

441
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:56,091
‪I'll just handle this case
‪on my own, like I always do.

442
00:27:56,174 --> 00:27:58,301
‪[stammering] Wait a minute, wait a minute.

443
00:27:58,385 --> 00:27:59,594
‪Uh, I don't see them,

444
00:27:59,677 --> 00:28:02,722
‪but even if I do, it's not like
‪it's my first time experiencing this.

445
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:04,265
‪I'm used to it by now.

446
00:28:05,308 --> 00:28:07,185
<i>‪I have my own ways</i>
<i>‪of dealing with them now.</i>

447
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:09,062
‪I'm not on your level,
‪but I'm not that bad.

448
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:11,147
‪Even so…

449
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:13,191
<i>‪And the truth is, I'm curious too.</i>

450
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:16,611
‪This centuries-old mystery
‪has really drawn me in.

451
00:28:16,694 --> 00:28:18,238
‪I have to see how it ends.

452
00:28:21,574 --> 00:28:22,826
‪Okay, sounds good.

453
00:28:22,909 --> 00:28:25,703
‪But you have to call me
‪the second anything happens, got it?

454
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,497
‪Okay.

455
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,335
‪Sleep well.

456
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:33,336
‪[phone beeps]

457
00:28:40,927 --> 00:28:42,971
‪[upbeat, romantic music playing]

458
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,378
‪[Gang-uk] <i>‪No sign of them.</i>
<i>‪No need to worry.</i>

459
00:29:58,004 --> 00:29:58,963
‪PROSECUTOR MA

460
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:00,340
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Great, I'm glad.</i>

461
00:30:04,552 --> 00:30:05,428
‪[Baek] Come in.

462
00:30:07,764 --> 00:30:08,890
‪You wanted to see me?

463
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:15,772
‪Here, let's have a cup of tea.

464
00:30:15,855 --> 00:30:18,483
‪You're more of a coffee person,
‪though, aren't you?

465
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:22,695
‪Hmm. Well, um, I'm staying away
‪from caffeine for now.

466
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:26,157
‪Come to think of it,
‪you look a little pale right now.

467
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:28,243
‪What happened? You're not sick, are you?

468
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:30,036
‪They said it's nothing specific.

469
00:30:30,119 --> 00:30:31,788
‪[chuckles] At my age,

470
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:33,540
‪that's the best you can get.

471
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:36,751
‪I'm sorry to hear that.

472
00:30:37,669 --> 00:30:38,920
‪I haven't been calling you.

473
00:30:39,003 --> 00:30:40,421
‪I'll do that more often now.

474
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:42,131
‪Great.

475
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:46,594
‪Yeo-ri, I'd rather you came by more often.

476
00:30:46,678 --> 00:30:47,971
‪[chuckles]

477
00:30:48,847 --> 00:30:51,224
‪Instead of waiting
‪for me to call you over.

478
00:30:56,229 --> 00:30:57,897
‪Yeah, that was 12 years ago.

479
00:30:57,981 --> 00:30:59,148
‪He had a heart transplant.

480
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:00,984
‪But I don't see
‪anything else other than that.

481
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:07,282
‪Of course. I'm telling you because I know
‪the donor's identity is confidential.

482
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:10,410
‪How long will it take?

483
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:15,832
‪Yeah. ASAP.

484
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:25,842
‪PRELIMINARY BACKGROUND CHECK REPORT
‪SUBJECT: MA GANG-UK

485
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:28,386
‪[doctor] 200 joules.

486
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:29,512
‪[nurse] 200 joules.

487
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:30,430
‪-[doctor] Clear.
‪-[thumps]

488
00:31:30,513 --> 00:31:32,098
‪[alarm beeping]

489
00:31:33,182 --> 00:31:34,726
‪-[defibrillator surges]
‪-[doctor] Clear.

490
00:31:34,809 --> 00:31:37,020
‪[nurse]
‪The donor's heart has been removed, sir.

491
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:01,628
‪[heart beating]

492
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,347
‪[groaning]

493
00:32:18,811 --> 00:32:20,063
‪[Hwa-yong lecturing faintly on phone]

494
00:32:20,146 --> 00:32:21,731
‪-Pil-dong?
‪-Hmm?

495
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:23,358
‪Option one or option two?

496
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:25,443
‪-Hmm, just two?
‪-Yeah.

497
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:27,904
‪-Option one.
‪-Okay, donkkaseu.

498
00:32:27,987 --> 00:32:29,030
‪-[both laugh]
‪-Of course.

499
00:32:29,113 --> 00:32:30,531
‪[Hwa-yong] <i>‪…violence is committed</i>
<i>‪in the name of love…</i>

500
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,909
‪-Donkkaseu, cool.
<i>‪-…we made the decision to make this letter</i>

501
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:35,119
<i>‪-available to the public…</i>
‪-Hey. Wanna grab lunch?

502
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,496
‪-You go ahead.
‪-[Hyeong-min] Are you sure?

503
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:39,165
‪-We're getting donkkaseu.
‪-[Gang-uk] Enjoy.

504
00:32:39,248 --> 00:32:42,919
‪[Hwa-yong] <i>‪After we finally release it,</i>
<i>‪I intend to donate it in accordance…</i>

505
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:44,170
‪LEE HWA-YONG,
‪DIRECTOR OF YEEON FOUNDATION

506
00:32:44,253 --> 00:32:45,713
<i>‪…with the last and final wishes</i>
<i>‪of my late father,</i>

507
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:47,465
<i>‪first director of the Yeeon Foundation,</i>

508
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:49,592
<i>‪to my alma mater.</i>‪ [chuckles]

509
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:53,680
‪That's right.
‪I heard the founding chairman

510
00:32:53,763 --> 00:32:56,933
‪donated just about all the old records
‪on Kang Pyeong-gun to his old university.

511
00:32:57,016 --> 00:32:59,769
‪Well, every investigation's
‪gotta start somewhere, right?

512
00:32:59,852 --> 00:33:04,148
‪And these Kang Pyeong-gun records might
‪just lead us exactly where we need to go.

513
00:33:04,232 --> 00:33:06,776
‪So, I'm thinking I'll swing by after work.

514
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:09,696
‪Oh. I was actually planning to go there.

515
00:33:09,779 --> 00:33:11,614
‪Oh! Well, let's go together.

516
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:13,533
‪Okay, sure.

517
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:26,754
‪-Mr. Bong.
‪-Yes?

518
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,297
‪Come a little closer.

519
00:33:30,633 --> 00:33:32,719
‪About this afternoon's executive meeting,

520
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:33,928
‪anything special on the agenda?

521
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:36,723
‪Uh, no, not particularly, ma'am.

522
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:39,726
‪Okay, well, in that case, you're going
‪to be running the meeting yourself.

523
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:47,775
‪Yes.

524
00:33:50,903 --> 00:33:52,905
‪Oh. Hey, Ms. Eom.

525
00:33:53,656 --> 00:33:56,743
‪Do you think Ms. Cheon's
‪been acting a little strange lately?

526
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:58,494
‪Yes I do, Mr. Bong. You noticed too?

527
00:33:58,578 --> 00:34:00,747
‪Ah. I knew you'd be
‪the right person to ask.

528
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:05,418
‪I guess so. She's been a little
‪less guarded than she used to be, right?

529
00:34:05,501 --> 00:34:06,544
‪You know what?

530
00:34:06,627 --> 00:34:09,297
‪I feel like she's more trusting now.
‪She's letting people in.

531
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:11,215
‪Especially this guy.

532
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:15,720
‪Ah! You saw what happened in there.
‪She went and singled me out.

533
00:34:15,803 --> 00:34:18,306
‪She said, "Mr. Bong,
‪come a little closer."

534
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:20,725
‪And then she left
‪the executive meeting in my hands.

535
00:34:20,808 --> 00:34:22,810
‪[laughing] It's clear as day by now.

536
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,271
‪What is clear?

537
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,940
‪Well, that she sees me as her right-hand.

538
00:34:28,024 --> 00:34:29,859
‪[laughing]

539
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:33,863
‪Too much pressure for one person.

540
00:34:33,946 --> 00:34:35,907
‪[laughing]

541
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:38,785
‪Do you want to know
‪what's "too much," Mr. Bong? You are.

542
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:41,537
‪Ah. You're just jealous.
‪I'm an easygoing guy. [chuckling]

543
00:34:41,621 --> 00:34:42,914
‪[door opens]

544
00:34:45,708 --> 00:34:47,627
‪[Gang-uk] Yeah. Yes, I'm here.

545
00:34:47,710 --> 00:34:49,253
‪Sure, sounds great. Thanks!

546
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:51,339
‪He put in a word for us.

547
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:54,383
‪Oh, right.

548
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:56,094
‪Rule number two, right?

549
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:58,596
‪Keep a safe distance. Sorry.

550
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:01,641
‪[sighs] The weather's amazing, isn't it?

551
00:35:03,476 --> 00:35:06,062
‪I think my balance is off.
‪I keep pulling to the left.

552
00:35:06,145 --> 00:35:07,480
‪[both chuckle]

553
00:35:10,024 --> 00:35:11,484
‪-Welcome.
‪-Hello.

554
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:13,778
‪I just talked to my boss on the phone.

555
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:16,280
‪-He told me to help you out however I can.
‪-We appreciate it.

556
00:35:16,364 --> 00:35:18,116
‪-This way, Ms. Cheon.
‪-Mm-hmm.

557
00:35:30,920 --> 00:35:32,880
‪[Gang-uk]
‪So many old documents in here, huh?

558
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:33,965
‪[chuckles]

559
00:35:35,174 --> 00:35:37,552
‪This is the Yeeon Foundation section.

560
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:39,303
‪All donated documents are here.

561
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:47,770
‪Is that Kang Pyeong-gun's?

562
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:52,400
‪This is a record of property inheritance
‪the king issued to Lord Kang Pyeong-gun.

563
00:35:52,483 --> 00:35:54,026
‪Kang Pyeong-gun's name is right here.

564
00:35:54,652 --> 00:35:57,446
‪It specifies every room,
‪even the number of kitchen bays.

565
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:58,865
‪It's more detailed than I thought.

566
00:35:59,907 --> 00:36:01,993
‪Ah, is there something like

567
00:36:02,076 --> 00:36:03,703
‪a blueprint of the house or a floor plan?

568
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:06,455
‪There is something along
‪those lines. It's called a <i>‪Jetaekdo.</i>

569
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,877
‪This was Kang Pyeong-gun's residence.

570
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:15,214
‪Wow. Is it okay
‪if I take a picture of this?

571
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:24,473
‪Wow.

572
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:28,769
‪This is Kang Pyeong-gun's
‪personal anthology.

573
00:36:29,478 --> 00:36:31,647
‪You could think of it
‪as a collection of essays.

574
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:32,565
‪HWAPYEONG ANTHOLOGY

575
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:37,486
‪So we have these
‪and the records about his home.

576
00:36:37,570 --> 00:36:38,946
‪Do you have anything else here?

577
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:41,115
‪There's one more,
‪his personal travel journal.

578
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:42,241
‪Give me a moment.

579
00:36:45,828 --> 00:36:47,914
‪Oh! Yeo-ri, wait a minute.

580
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:48,956
‪Hmm?

581
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:51,626
‪Oh, watch out!

582
00:36:54,587 --> 00:36:56,589
‪-What are you doing? Be careful.
‪-Oh, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

583
00:37:01,844 --> 00:37:02,678
‪Huh?

584
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:06,766
‪What's that?

585
00:37:23,157 --> 00:37:24,242
‪Take… Take a picture.

586
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:30,915
‪[camera shutter clicking]

587
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:37,880
‪"The camellia tree
‪by my late wife's grave."

588
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:41,759
‪That has to be a reference to
‪where Hwagyeongdang was buried,

589
00:37:41,842 --> 00:37:44,553
‪-don't you think?
‪-Yeah, I think so too.

590
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:48,224
‪"I will look upon it for the rest of
‪my days to find comfort for my heartache."

591
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,310
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪Wait a second, so that means</i>

592
00:37:51,394 --> 00:37:54,772
<i>‪Hwagyeongdang's camellia tree</i>
<i>‪was visible from his residence, right?</i>

593
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:58,276
‪[Gang-uk] <i>‪And since Yeeon now stands</i>

594
00:37:58,359 --> 00:38:01,612
<i>‪on the old site</i>
<i>‪of Kang Pyeong-gun's residence…</i>

595
00:38:08,869 --> 00:38:10,121
‪Well, there you go.

596
00:38:10,204 --> 00:38:11,998
‪There's no such thing as a perfect crime.

597
00:38:12,999 --> 00:38:14,333
‪Even after so long,

598
00:38:15,167 --> 00:38:17,044
‪the truth always ends up coming out.

599
00:38:19,547 --> 00:38:20,965
‪Such a horrible obsession.

600
00:38:24,468 --> 00:38:25,970
‪Anyway, we've got a problem.

601
00:38:26,053 --> 00:38:27,722
‪There's no way
‪we can check under the tree.

602
00:38:28,347 --> 00:38:29,682
‪We can't just dig it up.

603
00:38:29,765 --> 00:38:31,350
‪It belongs to the museum.

604
00:38:31,434 --> 00:38:33,019
‪Yeah, I know. Ugh.

605
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:34,437
‪And we can't just be honest about it,

606
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:35,896
‪because they'd think
‪we're completely nuts.

607
00:38:36,647 --> 00:38:39,525
‪Plus, this would be
‪a disgrace to their ancestors,

608
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:41,736
‪so that is not an option.

609
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:45,031
‪We'll have to find a way
‪to make it happen somehow.

610
00:38:46,198 --> 00:38:47,325
‪Hwagyeongdang…

611
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:50,328
‪really needs to be set free.

612
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,040
‪Yeah.

613
00:38:55,124 --> 00:38:56,208
‪[sighs]

614
00:38:58,461 --> 00:39:00,212
‪Is that Cheon Yeo-ri, or am I wrong?

615
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:03,883
‪And who is that man?

616
00:39:06,552 --> 00:39:08,095
‪Director Ok, hi.

617
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:11,474
<i>‪Is Cheon Yeo-ri interested</i>
<i>‪in the gallery, by any chance?</i>

618
00:39:11,557 --> 00:39:13,184
‪She's been coming here a lot lately.

619
00:39:13,267 --> 00:39:14,727
‪Cheon Yeo-ri?

620
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:16,479
‪Has she been asking questions

621
00:39:16,562 --> 00:39:19,106
‪about the hotel's artwork
‪or anything like that?

622
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:20,232
‪No, nothing like that.

623
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:23,277
‪She's just here with some guy right now.

624
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:24,820
‪Oh, I see. [chuckles]

625
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:29,033
‪And the guy she's with,
‪does it happen to be Kang Min-hwan?

626
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:31,410
‪[Hwa-yong] <i>‪No way.</i>
<i>‪I'd recognize Min-hwan in a heartbeat.</i>

627
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:34,205
‪And also,
‪he'd definitely stop by to say hello.

628
00:39:34,288 --> 00:39:35,581
‪[Gye-hui chuckles] Right.

629
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:39,460
‪Anyway, I'll try to drop by
‪sometime soon to see you.

630
00:39:39,543 --> 00:39:41,337
‪There's something I need to tell you.

631
00:39:41,420 --> 00:39:43,297
‪Great, I hope it's good news, right?

632
00:39:43,381 --> 00:39:45,049
‪Ah, yes. [chuckles]

633
00:39:46,675 --> 00:39:48,552
‪-Mom.
‪-Hmm?

634
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:49,720
‪What did Ms. Lee say?

635
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:51,722
‪Were Yeo-ri and Min-hwan there together?

636
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:54,392
‪I don't think it was him, actually. No.

637
00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:59,063
‪Are Cheon Yeo-ri and Min-hwan
‪actually seeing each other?

638
00:39:59,146 --> 00:40:00,648
‪You saw the other article, right?

639
00:40:01,357 --> 00:40:02,775
‪They're not dating yet.

640
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:05,027
‪Don't say "yet." Come on.

641
00:40:05,111 --> 00:40:06,654
‪That makes it sound like they will date.

642
00:40:07,613 --> 00:40:10,157
‪Mom, if Min-hwan and Yeo-ri get married,

643
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:12,910
‪that leaves us
‪in a terrible position, doesn't it?

644
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:18,290
‪[groans]

645
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:21,127
‪We'll just have to play that card again
‪if it doesn't pan out.

646
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,546
‪You mean that thing about the ghosts?

647
00:40:23,629 --> 00:40:26,424
‪We can't play that card, all right?
‪We can't prove that.

648
00:40:27,007 --> 00:40:29,051
‪People are already spreading rumors.

649
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:32,721
‪I heard they came from Cha Gi-u's side
‪after the engagement ended.

650
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:34,098
‪-Hey, wait…
‪-Huh?

651
00:40:34,181 --> 00:40:35,766
‪Is Cha Gi-u back in Korea?

652
00:40:35,850 --> 00:40:36,976
‪Huh? Oh, yeah.

653
00:40:37,059 --> 00:40:38,352
‪Came back last month, I heard.

654
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:39,437
‪Okay.

655
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:42,857
‪[Gong-jun] Oh! Look! I won!
‪Where are you going?

656
00:40:43,899 --> 00:40:45,359
‪[scoffs] She's making a run for it.

657
00:40:48,195 --> 00:40:49,780
‪So you want the real reason?

658
00:40:53,534 --> 00:40:55,828
‪There isn't a "real" reason
‪and a "fake" reason, is there?

659
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:59,248
‪I wanna know what really happened,
‪not the PR version.

660
00:40:59,331 --> 00:41:02,001
‪People said you went abroad to study
‪as soon as it was called off.

661
00:41:03,919 --> 00:41:05,838
‪I heard the rumors you've been spreading.

662
00:41:05,921 --> 00:41:08,507
‪And the thing is,
‪they line up with my theory, so…

663
00:41:10,217 --> 00:41:11,886
‪And what's your theory, Ms. Cheon?

664
00:41:11,969 --> 00:41:15,139
‪I think, maybe there was
‪something about my cousin

665
00:41:15,222 --> 00:41:16,932
‪that was too much for you to handle, huh?

666
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:20,060
‪Something I couldn't handle?

667
00:41:20,936 --> 00:41:23,314
‪-Like what, Ms. Cheon?
‪-Well, you know…

668
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,192
‪Something involving ghosts
‪and the supernatural.

669
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:33,240
‪I'd like you to testify to that.

670
00:41:34,074 --> 00:41:35,618
‪When the time comes, all right?

671
00:41:42,791 --> 00:41:44,126
‪What happens then?

672
00:41:48,547 --> 00:41:51,091
‪[Ko] No, they were just working
‪on the place when they found it.

673
00:41:51,926 --> 00:41:53,677
‪-Yeah.
‪-[exhales]

674
00:41:53,761 --> 00:41:55,012
‪No. No, no. You can't.

675
00:41:55,095 --> 00:41:57,431
‪You'll end up in huge trouble
‪if you cover up an artifact like that.

676
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:59,808
‪Mm-hmm. Well, first things first,

677
00:41:59,892 --> 00:42:02,561
‪you need to report it.
‪I'll head over there.

678
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:04,355
‪I'll check it out. Maybe over the weekend.

679
00:42:04,438 --> 00:42:05,814
‪Uh-huh. I'm at work right now.

680
00:42:05,898 --> 00:42:07,942
‪Uh-huh. Hmm.

681
00:42:08,817 --> 00:42:09,944
‪Oh, boy.

682
00:42:10,027 --> 00:42:11,529
‪My parents are fixing up a wall
‪at their place,

683
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:14,448
‪and it turns out part of it was connected
‪to an old fortress site or something.

684
00:42:16,116 --> 00:42:17,952
‪-[Hyeong-min] They found an artifact?
‪-[Ko] Hmm.

685
00:42:18,035 --> 00:42:20,579
‪[Hyeong-min] I heard the government
‪pays you for that kinda stuff, right?

686
00:42:20,663 --> 00:42:21,622
‪Do you know how much?

687
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:23,457
‪[Ko] Yeah, well, I'm sure
‪it's peanuts anyway. Hey--

688
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:25,501
‪-You're always like that.
‪-Huh?

689
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:27,795
‪All… All you think about is money.

690
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,589
‪Well, everyone needs money
‪to survive, you know?

691
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:32,466
‪Sure. You know what else I need? Food.

692
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:34,385
‪-Team dinner tonight? What do you think?
‪-Oh!

693
00:42:34,468 --> 00:42:36,303
‪Let's have pork rind. How does that sound?

694
00:42:36,387 --> 00:42:38,430
‪-Next time, next time.
‪-Wait a second, hold on. Listen to me.

695
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:41,475
‪You are going to love this place.
‪They actually age it right there.

696
00:42:41,559 --> 00:42:43,686
‪-Aged pork rind. They do it right there.
‪-Cool. Next time, next time.

697
00:42:43,769 --> 00:42:45,646
‪You… I swear to God,
‪I'm sick of looking at his face.

698
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:47,398
‪I mean, you're really
‪something else, you know that?

699
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:49,483
‪Did I do something to you?

700
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:50,901
‪Always with your sharp exits.

701
00:42:50,985 --> 00:42:52,695
‪You're like cutting out of here
‪like a chef with a knife.

702
00:42:52,778 --> 00:42:54,113
‪You should do that too, actually.

703
00:42:54,989 --> 00:42:55,990
‪You too.

704
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:58,117
‪See what I mean? Come on…

705
00:43:00,869 --> 00:43:02,037
‪[sighs]

706
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:03,998
‪I bet this is all because of a lady.

707
00:43:04,081 --> 00:43:06,834
‪Right? You know who, huh?

708
00:43:07,501 --> 00:43:09,712
‪Oh, right! Yeah. Uh-huh. Okay.

709
00:43:09,795 --> 00:43:12,214
‪Yeah. That girl, right?
‪That woman is probably out there.

710
00:43:12,298 --> 00:43:13,340
‪[Hyeong-min] <i>‪Mm-hmm.</i>

711
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:15,134
‪[Ko] <i>‪The only person who can turn Gang-uk</i>

712
00:43:15,217 --> 00:43:17,678
<i>‪into the king of leaving work on the dot:</i>

713
00:43:17,761 --> 00:43:20,139
<i>‪his grandmother, Mrs. Pang Myo-sun.</i>

714
00:43:20,222 --> 00:43:22,224
‪[slow, romantic music playing]

715
00:43:53,672 --> 00:43:56,091
‪Yeo-ri. You're here early.

716
00:43:56,175 --> 00:43:57,801
‪[sighs] Gang-uk.

717
00:43:57,885 --> 00:44:00,471
‪Oh, I'm a little early.

718
00:44:00,554 --> 00:44:02,056
‪But you're a little early too.

719
00:44:02,139 --> 00:44:04,642
‪Ah. I wanted to be the first one here.
‪I was a minute too late.

720
00:44:04,725 --> 00:44:06,226
‪[both chuckle]

721
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:09,396
‪It's nice being here, huh?
‪Makes me feel like I'm back in school.

722
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:13,067
‪Yeah. And it's quiet,
‪so we won't run into anyone we know.

723
00:44:13,150 --> 00:44:16,070
‪Ah! Listen, I came up with an idea

724
00:44:16,153 --> 00:44:18,197
‪-so we can search under the tree.
‪-Did you?

725
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:20,783
‪If you find an artifact
‪while building on private property,

726
00:44:20,866 --> 00:44:22,534
‪you're required to stop construction.

727
00:44:22,618 --> 00:44:23,869
‪Cultural Heritage Law. Yup!

728
00:44:23,952 --> 00:44:26,413
‪-Oh, that's right. You would know.
‪-[chuckles]

729
00:44:27,289 --> 00:44:28,457
‪In any case,

730
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,709
‪if that's our move,

731
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:32,586
‪I need to pull out my ace in the hole.

732
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:33,879
‪Hmm?

733
00:44:36,298 --> 00:44:40,386
‪[Hwa-yong] Hold on.
‪You want to buy our camellia tree?

734
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:43,597
‪You mentioned it last time.

735
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:44,807
‪Even in the south,

736
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:47,267
‪camellias with that bright
‪magenta color are hard to find.

737
00:44:48,352 --> 00:44:49,311
‪I want it for myself.

738
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:53,816
‪You know what? Honestly,

739
00:44:53,899 --> 00:44:55,401
‪I thought you were coming here so often

740
00:44:55,484 --> 00:44:57,069
‪because you were interested
‪in the business.

741
00:44:57,152 --> 00:44:59,029
‪-[both chuckle]
‪-But this is unexpected.

742
00:44:59,738 --> 00:45:02,157
‪Actually, some of the other things
‪you've shown interest in

743
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:03,617
‪have been a little unusual too.

744
00:45:03,700 --> 00:45:07,121
‪-You think so?
‪-Oh. Let me think here…

745
00:45:08,288 --> 00:45:11,083
‪Well, this camellia
‪meant a lot to my late father.

746
00:45:11,166 --> 00:45:12,751
‪He spent years taking care of it.

747
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:14,878
‪And our visitors seem to love it too.

748
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:17,881
‪People are always in front of it,
‪taking pictures and all that.

749
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:19,049
‪I don't really see why--

750
00:45:19,133 --> 00:45:21,009
‪I wanna keep it at home, you know?

751
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,095
‪Put it in my yard, so I can always see it.

752
00:45:23,846 --> 00:45:26,390
‪Oh, but you can come here
‪whenever you want.

753
00:45:27,724 --> 00:45:28,725
‪Hmm…

754
00:45:29,309 --> 00:45:31,728
‪Wait a minute,
‪if you don't want to sell it to me,

755
00:45:31,812 --> 00:45:33,605
‪how about a trade instead?

756
00:45:34,231 --> 00:45:35,691
‪Uh, for what?

757
00:45:35,774 --> 00:45:39,361
‪Well, our family has
‪a really rare pine tree, it's very old.

758
00:45:40,988 --> 00:45:42,322
‪Is that so? Huh.

759
00:45:42,406 --> 00:45:45,909
‪You and Director Ok have been
‪really close lately, haven't you?

760
00:45:45,993 --> 00:45:49,121
‪Well, you know,
‪we're in the same line of work after all.

761
00:45:50,747 --> 00:45:53,000
‪She'll know what pine tree it is.

762
00:45:53,083 --> 00:45:55,294
‪Talk to her about it,
‪if you want. She'll tell you.

763
00:45:56,503 --> 00:45:58,046
‪Maybe she's already told you.

764
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:00,674
‪[phone buzzing]

765
00:46:02,468 --> 00:46:03,927
‪Ms. Lee, hi.

766
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:07,973
‪So you talked to Director Ok on the phone?

767
00:46:09,641 --> 00:46:10,601
‪Great.

768
00:46:11,268 --> 00:46:13,562
‪Then I'll prepare for the work on my end.

769
00:46:13,645 --> 00:46:14,980
‪Bye.

770
00:46:15,063 --> 00:46:16,440
‪[chuckles]

771
00:46:17,441 --> 00:46:18,775
‪[phone buzzing]

772
00:46:19,902 --> 00:46:20,903
‪Hmm?

773
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:22,863
‪Yes, hello?

774
00:46:27,201 --> 00:46:28,535
‪I'll be right there, thank you.

775
00:46:32,581 --> 00:46:33,665
‪Hi, Yeo-ri.

776
00:46:33,749 --> 00:46:35,584
‪I checked with the Korea Heritage Service,

777
00:46:35,667 --> 00:46:37,127
‪and it looks like
‪we can proceed as planned.

778
00:46:37,920 --> 00:46:39,087
‪That's great.

779
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:42,883
‪-Yeo-ri?
<i>‪-Yes?</i>

780
00:46:42,966 --> 00:46:45,552
‪Is everything okay? You seem…

781
00:46:45,636 --> 00:46:47,721
<i>‪Sorry about that.</i>
<i>‪I'm gonna have to call you back.</i>

782
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:01,527
‪Good evening.

783
00:47:03,070 --> 00:47:03,904
‪Go ahead.

784
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:19,086
‪[somber music playing]

785
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:22,756
‪You're here.

786
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:32,641
‪Grandma, hi.

787
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:37,479
‪What's going on? How are you?

788
00:47:37,563 --> 00:47:40,941
‪Nothing, I just had
‪a little spell, honey, that's all.

789
00:47:42,859 --> 00:47:44,319
‪I was lucky Min-hwan was there.

790
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:47,406
‪He called an ambulance
‪before anything worse happened.

791
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:50,993
‪No one else knows about this.

792
00:47:51,076 --> 00:47:53,287
‪Especially not Director Ok.

793
00:47:55,706 --> 00:47:57,207
‪Oh, Grandma…

794
00:48:17,060 --> 00:48:19,313
‪I'm not dead yet, you know?

795
00:48:19,396 --> 00:48:21,898
‪Goodness, this isn't like you.

796
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:24,443
‪Hmm.

797
00:48:30,574 --> 00:48:31,617
‪I'm so sorry.

798
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:33,994
‪[music continues]

799
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:38,790
‪I'll go check on Ms. Cheon.

800
00:49:00,979 --> 00:49:02,147
‪[sighs]

801
00:49:02,939 --> 00:49:04,608
‪I wonder if everything's all right.

802
00:49:08,570 --> 00:49:09,988
‪Maybe I should go to her place?

803
00:49:13,241 --> 00:49:14,576
‪No, too much.

804
00:49:26,588 --> 00:49:29,007
‪I didn't want to mention this,
‪for your sake.

805
00:49:30,092 --> 00:49:33,387
‪But I don't really know
‪how much time I have left.

806
00:49:33,470 --> 00:49:35,389
‪What do you mean?
‪What are you talking about?

807
00:49:36,598 --> 00:49:40,560
‪You know what I was
‪most worried about after I collapsed?

808
00:49:40,644 --> 00:49:41,812
‪Cheon Yeo-ri.

809
00:49:41,895 --> 00:49:43,730
‪"I can't leave her all by herself."

810
00:49:44,815 --> 00:49:46,858
‪Cha Gi-u, your ex-fiancé.

811
00:49:47,734 --> 00:49:51,279
‪He's been spreading rumors about
‪why you called off the wedding.

812
00:49:52,781 --> 00:49:54,241
‪Bury this story with a bigger one.

813
00:49:55,242 --> 00:49:58,537
‪This is our chance
‪to prove them all wrong.

814
00:49:59,663 --> 00:50:02,666
‪Yeo-ri, let's put the gossip to rest.

815
00:50:02,749 --> 00:50:05,419
‪You must announce
‪the engagement to Min-hwan.

816
00:50:06,420 --> 00:50:09,339
‪I'll admit it, this battle
‪for ownership will be tough.

817
00:50:09,423 --> 00:50:11,758
‪I know they've got
‪plenty of support right now.

818
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:14,302
‪But doing that would
‪only treat the symptoms.

819
00:50:14,386 --> 00:50:16,847
‪That approach isn't going to fix
‪what's really wrong.

820
00:50:16,930 --> 00:50:18,890
‪I'll show them what I'm capable of,

821
00:50:19,683 --> 00:50:21,935
‪and I'll win the shareholders' trust,
‪I promise you.

822
00:50:22,018 --> 00:50:23,562
‪[chuckles]

823
00:50:24,479 --> 00:50:27,149
‪The issue here is time.

824
00:50:32,028 --> 00:50:35,115
‪I have to start
‪the succession process right away.

825
00:50:35,198 --> 00:50:37,659
‪You remember Director Gong
‪and Director Jang, don't you?

826
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:39,536
‪They were really close
‪with the late chairman.

827
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:41,955
‪They have enough shares between them

828
00:50:42,038 --> 00:50:43,248
‪to hold the deciding vote.

829
00:50:43,331 --> 00:50:45,459
‪As far as I remember,
‪they've always been neutral.

830
00:50:45,542 --> 00:50:48,044
‪Yes. And that's exactly why

831
00:50:48,128 --> 00:50:50,255
‪we're going to approach
‪Director Jang first.

832
00:50:50,964 --> 00:50:54,342
‪Chairwoman Baek
‪wants to formalize the succession

833
00:50:54,426 --> 00:50:56,303
‪at the next shareholders' meeting.

834
00:50:56,928 --> 00:50:59,389
‪Your mother loved Reina so much, you know?

835
00:51:00,015 --> 00:51:02,476
‪And Siena, but that goes without saying.

836
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:05,520
‪If you want to protect them,

837
00:51:05,604 --> 00:51:07,063
‪then I'm begging you,

838
00:51:07,147 --> 00:51:09,274
‪listen to me this time around.

839
00:51:09,357 --> 00:51:10,817
‪Remember last time?

840
00:51:10,901 --> 00:51:13,278
‪The stock jumped
‪as soon as the article dropped.

841
00:51:14,362 --> 00:51:15,822
‪Min-hwan will have your back.

842
00:51:16,531 --> 00:51:18,742
‪He'll be valuable to you in many ways.

843
00:51:19,534 --> 00:51:21,244
‪You've known him since you were kids.

844
00:51:22,204 --> 00:51:23,497
‪[chuckles]

845
00:51:33,048 --> 00:51:34,466
‪[sighs]

846
00:51:35,550 --> 00:51:36,760
‪[phone buzzes]

847
00:51:41,223 --> 00:51:42,974
‪Gosh, Yeo-ri, why has it been so…

848
00:51:44,100 --> 00:51:46,478
‪It's been so hard to reach you.
‪You said you'd call me later.

849
00:51:47,062 --> 00:51:48,939
‪Is, uh… Is everything okay?

850
00:51:49,523 --> 00:51:53,527
‪My grandmother wasn't feeling well,
‪so I went to visit her at the hospital.

851
00:51:53,610 --> 00:51:55,570
‪Oh. I'm sorry. Is she okay?

852
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:58,114
‪She's all right. She's doing better now.

853
00:51:58,198 --> 00:51:59,324
<i>‪That's a relief.</i>

854
00:51:59,407 --> 00:52:01,117
‪Are you okay, Yeo-ri?

855
00:52:01,785 --> 00:52:04,204
‪Yeah. By the way, I talked to Ms. Lee.

856
00:52:04,287 --> 00:52:06,081
‪She accepted. We closed the deal.

857
00:52:06,164 --> 00:52:07,874
‪We'll get it done
‪while the museum's closed.

858
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:09,501
‪Okay.

859
00:52:09,584 --> 00:52:11,169
‪So I guess we should be good to go.

860
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:13,421
<i>‪-Yeah.</i>
‪-Yeo-ri.

861
00:52:14,422 --> 00:52:17,300
‪Shall we have a team dinner?
‪What do you say?

862
00:52:17,384 --> 00:52:19,928
‪I was thinking we could have ramen
‪by the Hangang River.

863
00:52:20,762 --> 00:52:21,596
‪We'll see, Gang-uk.

864
00:52:23,807 --> 00:52:25,725
‪Well, see you at the museum.

865
00:52:25,809 --> 00:52:27,227
<i>‪-Okay.</i>
‪-Bye.

866
00:52:39,447 --> 00:52:42,534
‪YEEON MUSEUM OF ART
‪TEMPORARY CLOSURE

867
00:52:42,617 --> 00:52:45,453
‪[thunder rumbling]

868
00:52:46,496 --> 00:52:48,623
‪Looks like we're in for some heavy rain.

869
00:52:48,707 --> 00:52:50,250
‪Ugh. Maybe we should do it
‪some other time.

870
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:53,503
‪What if Ms. Lee changes her mind
‪out of the blue?

871
00:52:53,587 --> 00:52:55,839
‪-Let's go ahead with it.
‪-Okay.

872
00:52:55,922 --> 00:52:57,048
‪Let's get started.

873
00:52:57,716 --> 00:52:59,676
‪Okay, come on, let's begin!

874
00:52:59,759 --> 00:53:01,052
‪-Yes, sir!
‪-Yes, sir!

875
00:53:01,803 --> 00:53:03,054
‪Let's start over here.

876
00:53:12,689 --> 00:53:14,733
‪I told them to dig deep.

877
00:53:14,816 --> 00:53:17,944
‪Once the coffin's exposed, we'll stop
‪the work immediately and call it in.

878
00:53:19,529 --> 00:53:21,239
‪Oh, the papers. Do we have all we need?

879
00:53:23,116 --> 00:53:27,162
‪I filled out the report ahead of time.
‪Everything's ready to go.

880
00:53:27,245 --> 00:53:28,413
‪Okay.

881
00:53:28,496 --> 00:53:31,583
‪Once we call it in,
‪they'll send someone to check it out.

882
00:53:32,292 --> 00:53:34,377
‪Before we know it,
‪they'll be out here inspecting the coffin.

883
00:53:37,088 --> 00:53:39,716
‪-[phone buzzing]
‪-[Hwa-yong] Director Ok, hello.

884
00:53:40,216 --> 00:53:42,302
‪They've just started digging.

885
00:53:42,928 --> 00:53:44,804
‪Yeah, I…

886
00:53:44,888 --> 00:53:46,890
‪Is it just me, or does something feel off?

887
00:53:47,515 --> 00:53:48,642
‪To be honest,

888
00:53:49,225 --> 00:53:52,354
‪it's a beautiful tree,
‪but it's just a common camellia.

889
00:53:52,437 --> 00:53:55,273
‪Why would she trade
‪for such a valuable ancient tree?

890
00:53:57,233 --> 00:53:58,902
‪Doesn't that seem a little strange to you?

891
00:53:58,985 --> 00:54:00,320
‪[laughs]

892
00:54:00,403 --> 00:54:02,781
‪Maybe she's just obsessed
‪with that magenta color.

893
00:54:02,864 --> 00:54:04,616
‪[laughs] That's her.

894
00:54:04,699 --> 00:54:05,951
‪Yeo-ri's always been like that.

895
00:54:06,034 --> 00:54:09,663
‪Once her heart is set on something,
‪she won't stop until it's hers. [chuckles]

896
00:54:09,746 --> 00:54:11,790
‪Anyway, congrats on your purchase.

897
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:13,458
‪That's a really valuable tree,
‪so good for you.

898
00:54:15,168 --> 00:54:17,545
‪-Why, thank you.
‪-Bye.

899
00:54:20,632 --> 00:54:22,634
‪-[blowing]
‪-[phone buzzing]

900
00:54:23,343 --> 00:54:25,011
‪INCOMING CALL - SECRETARY WANG,
‪CHAIRWOMAN'S OFFICE

901
00:54:33,979 --> 00:54:36,815
‪[groans]
‪What happens if we don't find anything?

902
00:54:40,235 --> 00:54:43,029
‪Oh! It's raining.
‪Come on, Yeo-ri. Come on.

903
00:54:43,113 --> 00:54:44,656
‪-Get under the canopy!
‪-[foreman] Stop what you're doing…

904
00:54:44,739 --> 00:54:46,533
‪-[worker] Oh, it's pouring!
‪-…and get under the canopy.

905
00:54:47,492 --> 00:54:48,868
‪Come inside, come inside!

906
00:54:48,952 --> 00:54:50,120
‪Damn it, we barely started.

907
00:55:06,553 --> 00:55:09,180
‪Hey, what's with the family dinner?

908
00:55:09,264 --> 00:55:11,057
‪Are we in trouble or something?

909
00:55:11,141 --> 00:55:13,393
‪Ha-ri, was it you? What did you do?

910
00:55:13,476 --> 00:55:15,061
‪I didn't do anything.

911
00:55:15,145 --> 00:55:17,272
‪Well, never mind then.
‪Why'd you get so worked up?

912
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:19,607
‪It's no big deal,
‪just a family dinner, settle down.

913
00:55:19,691 --> 00:55:21,484
‪I don't buy that. I think it's weird.

914
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:23,903
‪Min-hwan was invited too. Oh, no.

915
00:55:23,987 --> 00:55:25,822
‪They're not about
‪to get engaged, are they?

916
00:55:27,240 --> 00:55:29,617
‪It would really suck for us if they did.

917
00:55:29,701 --> 00:55:31,494
‪Getting engaged is no simple task.

918
00:55:31,578 --> 00:55:33,580
‪Remember Cha Gi-u? That fell apart.

919
00:55:33,663 --> 00:55:36,207
‪They called it off
‪on the day of the wedding.

920
00:55:36,291 --> 00:55:39,711
‪That's true. Cheon Yeo-ri has a way
‪of messing things up for herself, right?

921
00:55:42,130 --> 00:55:43,798
‪They're not getting engaged tonight.

922
00:55:45,175 --> 00:55:46,301
‪How do you know that?

923
00:55:47,510 --> 00:55:50,472
‪Mommy, call Director Gong for a minute.

924
00:55:51,514 --> 00:55:54,476
‪It's not getting better.
‪We're gonna have to call it a day.

925
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:56,102
‪Yes, safety first, you're right.

926
00:55:56,186 --> 00:55:58,313
‪-Let's just call it for now.
‪-[phone buzzing]

927
00:55:58,396 --> 00:55:59,731
‪The weather's been crazy
‪these days, right?

928
00:55:59,814 --> 00:56:01,691
‪I know, man.
‪It's getting crazier every year.

929
00:56:03,234 --> 00:56:04,235
‪Grandma, hi.

930
00:56:06,321 --> 00:56:07,405
‪A family dinner?

931
00:56:10,617 --> 00:56:11,868
‪Min-hwan's going too?

932
00:56:16,790 --> 00:56:18,166
‪Okay, I'll be there.

933
00:56:21,628 --> 00:56:22,879
‪Yeo-ri, what's going on?

934
00:56:27,383 --> 00:56:28,259
‪I…

935
00:56:30,595 --> 00:56:32,347
‪think I'm going to have to get engaged.

936
00:56:34,557 --> 00:56:35,642
‪Huh?

937
00:56:36,476 --> 00:56:38,561
‪Uh, what do you mean?

938
00:56:41,523 --> 00:56:42,982
‪[thunderclap]

939
00:56:45,777 --> 00:56:47,695
‪[dramatic music playing]

940
00:57:40,373 --> 00:57:41,374
‪Good evening.

941
00:57:41,458 --> 00:57:44,169
‪-Oh, there you are.
‪-Hello. Hi.

942
00:57:45,420 --> 00:57:47,380
‪To think I'd see you here.

943
00:57:48,047 --> 00:57:48,923
‪Happy to be here.

944
00:57:50,592 --> 00:57:52,051
‪Great, shall we get started then?

945
00:57:52,886 --> 00:57:54,721
‪Actually, I have something to say
‪before we start.

946
00:57:54,804 --> 00:57:58,391
‪Hold on a minute.
‪Someone else will be joining us soon.

947
00:58:00,059 --> 00:58:01,811
‪We should wait till he's here.

948
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:06,441
‪Just tell me this.
‪Did you hold hands with my cousin?

949
00:58:08,860 --> 00:58:10,987
‪I'd like you to testify to that.

950
00:58:11,070 --> 00:58:12,822
‪When the time comes, all right?

951
00:58:14,657 --> 00:58:15,700
‪Who is it?

952
00:58:21,206 --> 00:58:22,207
‪We have one more guest.

953
00:59:01,329 --> 00:59:03,873
‪[upbeat music playing]

954
00:59:10,964 --> 00:59:11,965
‪Hello, everyone.

955
00:59:13,049 --> 00:59:14,509
‪I'm Ma Gang-uk. It's a pleasure.

956
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:30,316
‪Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk and I…

957
00:59:33,194 --> 00:59:34,445
‪are getting engaged.

958
00:59:34,529 --> 00:59:37,115
‪[music continues]

959
01:00:22,827 --> 01:00:25,747
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

960
01:00:25,830 --> 01:00:28,124
‪[Baek] <i>‪So it's not about business</i>
<i>‪with Prosecutor Ma?</i>

961
01:00:28,207 --> 01:00:30,168
‪You have feelings
‪for each other, is that true?

962
01:00:30,251 --> 01:00:33,880
‪I like Yeo-ri a lot.
‪We're getting engaged and I'm excited.

963
01:00:33,963 --> 01:00:35,965
‪Tell me something, dear.
‪What's your zodiac sign?

964
01:00:36,049 --> 01:00:37,717
‪-What?
‪-Your sign.

965
01:00:37,800 --> 01:00:38,760
‪[Yeo-ri] <i>‪My sign?</i>

966
01:00:38,843 --> 01:00:39,927
‪[Ko] <i>‪Okay then, next.</i>

967
01:00:40,553 --> 01:00:42,305
‪-[Gang-uk] Back then…
‪-I was playing hard to get.

968
01:00:42,388 --> 01:00:44,724
‪You're gonna call off the engagement,
‪that's what you'll do.

969
01:00:45,308 --> 01:00:47,560
‪-You're kidding me.
‪-How about we work together?

970
01:00:47,644 --> 01:00:49,729
‪We both want to break them up,
‪and I know how to do it.

971
01:00:49,812 --> 01:00:52,106
‪[Gye-hui] <i>‪You remember</i>
<i>‪what happened six years ago, right?</i>

972
01:00:52,190 --> 01:00:55,401
‪I want to know the real reason
‪you broke off your engagement in exchange.

973
01:00:55,485 --> 01:00:57,528
‪[Baek] <i>‪I think you should have a meeting.</i>

974
01:00:57,612 --> 01:01:01,574
‪I think Director Ok has started openly
‪trying to keep you in check.

975
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:02,659
‪CIVIL SERVANT PERSONNEL RECORD
‪MA GANG-UK

976
01:01:02,742 --> 01:01:05,453
‪[Min-hwan] <i>‪Yeo-ri can never get engaged.</i>
<i>‪Not to Ma Gang-uk, or anyone else.</i>

977
01:01:05,536 --> 01:01:07,538
‪[Ha-ri] <i>‪I've got you now, Cheon Yeo-ri.</i>
